Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 48 CLINICAL DATA  51 year old female with increased cholesterol status post angioplasty times two on Prem pro for several years now with new left breast thickening  At 3 o clock  there is a very suspicious mass on mammo and ultrasound  Rule out malignancy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  CONSISTENT WITH DUCTAL ORIGIN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 57 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 AUG 98 at 15 56 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm aggregate of yellow white soft tan cores of tissue which are submitted in toto in cassette A  Gross Description by  Joe Serra Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Sujata Somani  M D  Priscilla Slanetz  M D  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Charles Allen Boucher  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY , Core_biopsy.
